cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BCDD, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "BCDD: Behavioural Contract-Driven Design"
abstract: >-
  BCDD is a textual specification language whose unit is the Capability State Contract (CSC): one boundary of a
  system described through requests, input and output events, observable states, and guarantees and assumptions,
  each stating how it is verified. The tool bcdd checks form, names, types and the structural closure of entities
  made of parts; bcdd-editor is a graphical editor around it.
